      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been conducting a longitudinal study on my own interoceptive responses in relation to market micro-structure, specifically looking for signs of neuro-stochastic coupling. i've observed that certain localized proprioceptive shifts—for example, a sudden change in perceived limb weight or a localized thermal fluctuation in my forearm—seem to have a high degree of synchronicity with spikes in order flow toxicity and sudden shifts in the VIX term structure.\n\ni want to formalize this into a rigorous signal-processing framework. can you help me design a protocol to quantify these \"somatic state vectors\"? specifically, i need a way to map the thermal delta and the proprioceptive intensity against high-frequency volatility metrics so i can determine if these biological shifts function as a legitimate, low-latency proxy for imminent liquidity regime changes.",
      "source": "evaluator",
